## 6. Current Aerial implementation notes

- The live `Aerial` class in `routines of volt` uses Party Cannon-inspired shot direction prediction and hitbox standoff targeting.
- It predicts the ball at `intercept_time`, derives `self.shot_vector`, applies `ShotSurfaceGeometry.adjust_aerial`, then computes a hitbox-aware `self.target`.
- Its current launch condition is in the `if self.jumping or not agent.me.airborne:` block. On the first grounded tick it sets `self.jumping = True` and starts the jump immediately; this is why it currently launches from the floor without a distinct ground acceleration phase.
- Current jump simulation adds first jump impulse/hold acceleration and optional second jump impulse; fast aerial holds the first jump then pulses the second jump. It then orients toward the predicted hitbox target and uses Party Cannon-style boost estimation / forward-projection boost control.
- The current live branch does not contain the earlier proposed ground-speed build phase. The first grounded tick enters the existing jump sequence immediately. Do not assume the old 0.38 s ground setup, 1150 forward-speed threshold, or 0.88 alignment threshold are present unless they are re-added and verified in the live file.

## 7. Known regressions / pitfalls to avoid

- NumPy Vector construction can fail with inhomogeneous shapes (e.g. `Vector(target_center)`); use consistent scalar components or the project's established constructor pattern.
- `targets[0]` may be None; validate before indexing/converting.
- Do not reference `tools` in a scope where it is not imported/defined.
- Initialize variables on every control-flow path (past `slice_n` before assignment).
- Clamp prediction slice indices; prior double-jump code indexed `slices[round(T*120)-1]` and could go out of range.
- Aerial state fields must be initialized in `__init__` before use (past error: missing `aerial_started`).
- Avoid undefined helper names such as `_centered_shot_vector` and unbound locals such as `vf`.
- Be careful with VirxERLU Vector3 iteration/constructor assumptions.
- Do not add unsupported car fields such as `on_ground` or `has_wheel_contact`.
- Changes to aerial finder/selection must not accidentally make jump_shot start aerialing.
- Changes to side-flip logic previously caused excessive backflips and lost tilt-back shots.
- The user has reverted failed aerial, wall, reset, and shot experiments; always fetch the current live source first.

