## 10. Upside-down front-wheel redirect (2026-11-14)

- The previous aerial-opponent race filter, aerial commitment lock, and untargeted teammate/chip fallback were reverted at the user's request. Do not reintroduce them unless explicitly requested.
- New `Redirect` is a subclass of `Aerial`, not a replacement for the normal Aerial. It reuses the existing Party Cannon shot-direction prediction, jump simulation, boost estimate, and aerial PD orientation controller.
- Select Redirect only for a goal-directed aerial when the predicted ball is airborne (currently z > 350) and behind the car in local coordinates (currently local y < -100).
- Redirect changes the car-centre contact target so the front wheel pair reaches the ball while the car is inverted. The orientation controller must use `defaultPD(..., upside_down=True)`.
- Untargeted aerials remain normal Aerial routines. This redirect is not a generic fallback or teammate pass.
- Current live branch did not contain the earlier ground-speed setup described in section 6 despite the older note; inspect the live class before assuming that change is present.
- Initial front-wheel contact offsets are geometric estimates (front axle at 34% of hitbox length; inverted wheel offset at half hitbox height). They require in-game tuning and have not been validated.
